From 73a87a00982ac16590f0a23713e11d024f4100c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlnode-foundry <mlnode-foundry@kaitaku.ai>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 20:14:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(api): raise MAX_UNHEALTHY_COUNT from 3 to 9999
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3-strike auto-shutdown was tuned for early-network conditions where a hung
manager pointed at corrupt state. With v0.2.13 + PoC v2 streaming workloads
on large MoE models, intermittent transient unhealth (cold-start warmup,
brief network blips) trips the kill-switch too often.

Raising to 9999 effectively disables the auto-shutdown — operators reset
manually via container restart when truly stuck. Same value used in every
2026-04 / 2026-05 PoC v2 experiment on MiniMax-M2.7, Kimi-K2.6, and
Qwen3-235B.
---
 mlnode/packages/api/src/api/watcher.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mlnode/packages/api/src/api/watcher.py b/mlnode/packages/api/src/api/watcher.py
index 67e401b..12fde90 100644
--- a/mlnode/packages/api/src/api/watcher.py
+++ b/mlnode/packages/api/src/api/watcher.py
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ from common.logger import create_logger
 
 logger = create_logger(__name__)
 
-MAX_UNHEALTHY_COUNT = 3
+MAX_UNHEALTHY_COUNT = 9999
 
 
 async def watch_managers(
-- 
2.48.1

